# User-First Gummy Box

Read:

1. `docs/USER_FIRST_GUMMY_BOX.md`
2. `plans/active/2026-07-26-user-first-gummy-box-cursor-addendum.md`
3. `docs/AUTOMATED_ACCEPTANCE.md`

## Locked product law

```text
A Gummy Box exists when Gummy OS opens.
GitHub and Google Drive are optional connections, never prerequisites.
```

Do not design any ordinary user flow that requires the user to:

- register a GitHub App;
- generate or paste a PEM key;
- locate App or installation IDs;
- create environment variables;
- configure Vercel, Cloudflare, OAuth clients, buckets, or databases;
- understand protocol vocabulary before adding a project.

## Default experience

Within five seconds the user understands:

```text
Gummy is a place to bring a project and get help finishing it.
```

Within ten seconds the user can choose:

```text
Add a project
Talk to Gummy
```

Open to one waiting assistant presence, not an architecture dashboard.

## Vocabulary

Keep exact protocol terms internally. Use ordinary language by default:

```text
Work Order       → What Glopper will do
Capability Grant → Permission needed
Task Lease       → Working on it
Return           → Your result
Receipt          → What happened / Activity
Gummy Box        → Your projects / Storage & sync
Master Control   → Access & control
```

Technical terms belong under Details, diagnostics, developer mode, evidence exports, schemas, and documentation.

## Storage

Preserve:

- IndexedDB/OPFS local-first operation;
- provider-neutral Box identity;
- explicit authority and revocation;
- source/result separation;
- truthful executor/provider/locality/cost evidence.

Target managed service:

```text
Cloudflare Worker + D1 + R2 + Durable Object per Box + Queues where justified
```

Never send permanent R2 or provider credentials to browser code.

## Connectors

Production GitHub and Drive integrations are platform-owned apps.

Users click Connect, consent, select a repository/file/folder, and return. They never create developer credentials.

The current founder-owned GitHub App is a test fixture, not the consumer onboarding model.

## Build discipline

Do not destabilize the active standalone proof while its acceptance is in progress. Implement this as the next bounded lane with feature flags and automated acceptance.

No founder regression checklist. The computer tests the computer.
